WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.425
Three-valued logic becomes easier when you inspect a
few important combinations TRUE

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.725
AND UNKNOWN is UNKNOWN because the unknown side
could still be false

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.338
FALSE AND UNKNOWN is definitely false because one
false value is enough

00:00:14.225 --> 00:00:17.838
TRUE OR UNKNOWN is definitely true because one true
value is enough

00:00:18.725 --> 00:00:22.150
FALSE OR UNKNOWN remains unknown because the unknown
side could still be

00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:27.700
true NOT UNKNOWN remains unknown Run the truth table
and scan the

00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:33.550
combinations You do not need to memorize every row
Instead ask

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:36.625
whether the known part of the expression is already
enough to determine

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:37.600
the final result
